      "writtenOn": "2022-12-13T15:41:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both Dawn and Metal backends handle aligning the buffer allocation size, but I wonder if we should just require the buffer manager\u0027s to be responsible for this, since they are already handling offset alignment?\n\nOn a semi-related note, DrawBufferManager currently only aligns offsets but maybe should also be aligning each sub-allocation\u0027s size as well? When it uses transfer buffer copies, the size should be aligned too. I think I will make that as a follow up change, including logic to handle zeroing the padded bytes.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "9a3baeffbebcc22bc0c52e2993b5d5e600b8bf45",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "38e3fdf4_6c1f07f1",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/mtl/MtlBuffer.mm",
